			"notes": "# Ji-AFK Cinematic v2.3.2\n\n---\n\n<p align=\"center\">\n  <img src=\"https://preview.redd.it/creeper-gif-i-made-i-gave-up-on-the-explosion-v0-64rdrjmesq761.gif?width=704&auto=webp&s=cb2cf08931ba28b85a08b6705a92dd9f91c13174\" width=\"90\"/>\n</p>\n\nA major immersion update introducing dedicated fishing and sleep cinematics, improved camera composition and expanded Minecraft version support.\n\n## Added\n\n- Added **Fishing Cinematics**, a new cinematic mode designed specifically for fishing.\n  - Cinematics can begin automatically after casting a fishing rod, with a configurable activation delay of **10 seconds by default**.\n  - Regular cinematic shots continue while waiting for a catch.\n  - When a fish approaches the hook, the camera automatically switches to a close fishing-focused composition.\n  - Mouse movement, clicks, retrieving the rod and casting again no longer interrupt the fishing cinematic.\n  - Walking or pressing **Esc** still exits the cinematic normally.\n\n- Added **Sleep Cinematics**, allowing cinematic presentation and black bars to remain active while sleeping.\n  - **Light Mode** keeps the sleeping interface and chat available.\n  - **Full Mode** hides the sleeping interface for a cleaner cinematic presentation.\n  - Designed to complement extended and immersive sleeping mods such as **Better Days** and **VO: True Sleep**.\n\n## Improved\n\n- Improved the balance between **player-focused and environment-focused shots**.\n- Configured camera percentages now produce a more accurate and consistent shot distribution.\n- Character and environment shots now frame their intended subjects more reliably.\n- Pressing **Esc** during a cinematic now closes the cinematic first instead of immediately opening the pause menu.\n- Improved fishing transitions when catching a fish and casting the rod again.\n\n## Fixed\n\n- Fixed cinematic black bars not displaying correctly while sleeping.\n- Fixed fishing cinematics being cancelled by mouse movement, left click, right click or retrieving the rod.\n- Fixed missing fish-approach camera framing on some Minecraft 1.21 versions.\n- Fixed crashes when activating fishing cinematics on Minecraft **1.21.11**.\n- Fixed world-loading crashes affecting Minecraft **26.1, 26.1.1 and 26.1.2**.\n- Improved compatibility across Minecraft **1.21–1.21.11** and **26.1–26.3**.\n\n---\n\n## This update is strongly recommended for all users."
		}
